<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Carus of Segeda</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. 153 BCE</span> · <a href="/centuries/2nd-century-bce">2nd century BCE</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Carus of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/segeda">Segeda</a> was a Celtiberian leader chosen by the Belli and allied peoples as their general in 153 BCE, when <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rome">Rome</a> attacked over the fortification of Segeda. According to Appian, he ambushed the army of the consul <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/quintus-fulvius-nobilior">Quintus Fulvius Nobilior</a> and killed about 6,000 <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/roman-empire">Romans</a>, but he was himself killed when Roman cavalry counter-attacked.</p></div>
